{"case_id": "cache-tiers-ranked", "trial": 1, "condition": "candidate", "runner": "x-gemini-3.1-high", "model": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "runner_sha256": "24cb0f83ed4563d12cd13efe43a94f602801e8757249f6758b98c81c8355483c", "cases_sha256": "f52b0e4983a2815e81bb5c003273844a54d4f981a486087bd8986a85f2d6653b", "style_sha256": "7ac0e9b2cec88eb23b8fa71910242c02cecfae607e65524b583d27557a61d4ea", "response": "1. **In-memory map**\nUse this first. It needs no extra infrastructure.\nTradeoffs: It offers the fastest reads but consumes application memory. Data drops on service restart. State stays local to one instance.\n\n2. **CDN**\nUse this for public HTTP responses.\nTradeoffs: It stops traffic before it hits the service. Invalidation takes time. It cannot cache internal application data.\n\n3. **Redis**\nUse this only if multiple instances must share state.\nTradeoffs: It survives service restarts and shares data globally. It adds a network hop and requires separate infrastructure maintenance.", "usage": {"input": 75049, "output": 1422, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 76471, "reasoningTokens": 1296, "cost": {"input": 0.15009799999999998, "output": 0.017064, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.16716199999999998}}, "cost_usd": 0.167162}
{"case_id": "auth-for-cli", "trial": 1, "condition": "candidate", "runner": "x-gemini-3.1-high", "model": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "runner_sha256": "24cb0f83ed4563d12cd13efe43a94f602801e8757249f6758b98c81c8355483c", "cases_sha256": "f52b0e4983a2815e81bb5c003273844a54d4f981a486087bd8986a85f2d6653b", "style_sha256": "7ac0e9b2cec88eb23b8fa71910242c02cecfae607e65524b583d27557a61d4ea", "response": "1. **OAuth device flow**\n   - Benefit: Enforces MFA and handles offboarding automatically via your identity provider.\n   - Tradeoff: Requires more code to handle the browser callback and token refresh.\n\n2. **Long-lived PATs**\n   - Benefit: Takes minutes to build.\n   - Tradeoff: Creates severe leak risks in dotfiles and shell history. Forces manual rotation.\n\n3. **mTLS certs**\n   - Benefit: Stops token theft completely.\n   - Tradeoff: Forces you to provision, distribute, and rotate 40 client certificates on user machines.", "usage": {"input": 75057, "output": 1316, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 76373, "reasoningTokens": 1189, "cost": {"input": 0.150114, "output": 0.015792, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.165906}}, "cost_usd": 0.165906}
{"case_id": "mysql84-upgrade", "trial": 1, "condition": "candidate", "runner": "x-gemini-3.1-high", "model": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "runner_sha256": "24cb0f83ed4563d12cd13efe43a94f602801e8757249f6758b98c81c8355483c", "cases_sha256": "f52b0e4983a2815e81bb5c003273844a54d4f981a486087bd8986a85f2d6653b", "style_sha256": "7ac0e9b2cec88eb23b8fa71910242c02cecfae607e65524b583d27557a61d4ea", "response": "The upgrade breaks the application if it uses removed authentication plugins or deprecated commands.\n\n* **Authentication**: MySQL 8.4 disables the `mysql_native_password` plugin. Connections fail if the database user or the application driver relies on it. Migrate users to `caching_sha2_password`.\n* **Removed commands**: MySQL 8.4 removes legacy replication commands. Calls to `SHOW MASTER STATUS` fail. Change these calls to `SHOW BINARY LOG STATUS`.\n* **Performance regressions**: Shopify discovered an index merge bug in MySQL 8.4.5. This causes high CPU usage for some queries.\n\nProvide the repository name to check for these commands and older drivers.", "usage": {"input": 79986, "output": 1675, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 81661, "reasoningTokens": 1533, "cost": {"input": 0.159972, "output": 0.0201, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.180072}}, "cost_usd": 0.180072}
{"case_id": "es721-upgrade", "trial": 1, "condition": "candidate", "runner": "x-gemini-3.1-high", "model": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "runner_sha256": "24cb0f83ed4563d12cd13efe43a94f602801e8757249f6758b98c81c8355483c", "cases_sha256": "f52b0e4983a2815e81bb5c003273844a54d4f981a486087bd8986a85f2d6653b", "style_sha256": "7ac0e9b2cec88eb23b8fa71910242c02cecfae607e65524b583d27557a61d4ea", "response": "Elastic supports rolling upgrades between minor versions. `searchbuddy` runs minor version upgrades in-place via a rolling restart.\n\nI cannot see your cluster. Check the cluster for deprecated features:\n\n```bash\ncurl \"http://<cluster-host>:9200/_migration/deprecations\"\n```\n\nNext: Test the rolling upgrade on a staging cluster.", "usage": {"input": 6575, "output": 2776, "cacheRead": 111185, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 120536, "reasoningTokens": 2700, "cost": {"input": 0.01315, "output": 0.033312, "cacheRead": 0.022237000000000003, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.06869900000000001}}, "cost_usd": 0.068699}
{"case_id": "flag-compact", "trial": 1, "condition": "candidate", "runner": "x-gemini-3.1-high", "model": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "runner_sha256": "24cb0f83ed4563d12cd13efe43a94f602801e8757249f6758b98c81c8355483c", "cases_sha256": "f52b0e4983a2815e81bb5c003273844a54d4f981a486087bd8986a85f2d6653b", "style_sha256": "7ac0e9b2cec88eb23b8fa71910242c02cecfae607e65524b583d27557a61d4ea", "response": "I have not found a `--compact` flag in Conveyor or Shipit. Name the specific release tool you use.\n\n`centaur-cli` uses `--compact` to output compact JSON (single line, no indentation). If you mean another tool, provide the command or the repository.", "usage": {"input": 36091, "output": 639, "cacheRead": 73615, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 110345, "cost": {"input": 0.072182, "output": 0.007668, "cacheRead": 0.014723000000000002, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.09457299999999999}}, "cost_usd": 0.094573}
{"case_id": "flag-purge", "trial": 1, "condition": "candidate", "runner": "x-gemini-3.1-high", "model": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "runner_sha256": "24cb0f83ed4563d12cd13efe43a94f602801e8757249f6758b98c81c8355483c", "cases_sha256": "f52b0e4983a2815e81bb5c003273844a54d4f981a486087bd8986a85f2d6653b", "style_sha256": "7ac0e9b2cec88eb23b8fa71910242c02cecfae607e65524b583d27557a61d4ea", "response": "The `--soft` flag sends a `Fastly-Soft-Purge: \"1\"` header to Fastly. It marks the cached item as stale instead of deleting it. Fastly serves the stale content to users while it fetches the new version in the background.", "usage": {"input": 98885, "output": 716, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 99601, "reasoningTokens": 662, "cost": {"input": 0.19777, "output": 0.008592, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.206362}}, "cost_usd": 0.206362}
{"case_id": "health-check-5s", "trial": 1, "condition": "candidate", "runner": "x-gemini-3.1-high", "model": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "runner_sha256": "24cb0f83ed4563d12cd13efe43a94f602801e8757249f6758b98c81c8355483c", "cases_sha256": "f52b0e4983a2815e81bb5c003273844a54d4f981a486087bd8986a85f2d6653b", "style_sha256": "7ac0e9b2cec88eb23b8fa71910242c02cecfae607e65524b583d27557a61d4ea", "response": "I have not seen your `nginx.conf`. I cannot tell if the zone blocks the monitor.\n\nNginx blocks a request when it exceeds the zone `rate`. A monitor hitting every 5 seconds sends 12 requests per minute. If your configured rate is lower than this, Nginx blocks it.\n\nShow me the `nginx.conf` file. I will check the `limit_req_zone` rate and the `/health` location block.", "usage": {"input": 75045, "output": 906, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 75951, "reasoningTokens": 812, "cost": {"input": 0.15009, "output": 0.010872, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.160962}}, "cost_usd": 0.160962}
{"case_id": "waf-status-probe", "trial": 1, "condition": "candidate", "runner": "x-gemini-3.1-high", "model": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "runner_sha256": "24cb0f83ed4563d12cd13efe43a94f602801e8757249f6758b98c81c8355483c", "cases_sha256": "f52b0e4983a2815e81bb5c003273844a54d4f981a486087bd8986a85f2d6653b", "style_sha256": "7ac0e9b2cec88eb23b8fa71910242c02cecfae607e65524b583d27557a61d4ea", "response": "The WAF allows a `/status` probe every 15 seconds.\n\nThe `edge_waf_intents` table has no enabled rate limits. The active tarpit rules target anonymous traffic on paths like `/checkout` and `/cart`. They do not match `/status`. Four requests per minute is too low to trigger anti-abuse filters.", "usage": {"input": 4651, "output": 1194, "cacheRead": 78454, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 84299, "reasoningTokens": 1123, "cost": {"input": 0.009302, "output": 0.014328, "cacheRead": 0.0156908, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.0393208}}, "cost_usd": 0.0393208}
{"case_id": "crash-stack-header", "trial": 1, "condition": "candidate", "runner": "x-gemini-3.1-high", "model": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "runner_sha256": "24cb0f83ed4563d12cd13efe43a94f602801e8757249f6758b98c81c8355483c", "cases_sha256": "f52b0e4983a2815e81bb5c003273844a54d4f981a486087bd8986a85f2d6653b", "style_sha256": "7ac0e9b2cec88eb23b8fa71910242c02cecfae607e65524b583d27557a61d4ea", "response": "Cause: The code accessed index `[3]` (the fourth element) of a 3-element slice or array. Go uses zero-based indexing. Valid indices are 0, 1, and 2.\n\nNext: Read the full stack trace in the logs to find the exact file and line number. \n\nFix: Guard the array access with a length check (`if index < len(items)`) or change the loop condition to use `<` instead of `<=`.", "usage": {"input": 75053, "output": 1331, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 76384, "reasoningTokens": 1232, "cost": {"input": 0.150106, "output": 0.015972, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.166078}}, "cost_usd": 0.166078}
{"case_id": "rotation-failed", "trial": 1, "condition": "candidate", "runner": "x-gemini-3.1-high", "model": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "runner_sha256": "24cb0f83ed4563d12cd13efe43a94f602801e8757249f6758b98c81c8355483c", "cases_sha256": "f52b0e4983a2815e81bb5c003273844a54d4f981a486087bd8986a85f2d6653b", "style_sha256": "7ac0e9b2cec88eb23b8fa71910242c02cecfae607e65524b583d27557a61d4ea", "response": "`/var/log/app/app.log.1` fails: `open /var/log/app/app.log.1: permission denied`.\n\nCause: The process rotating the logs lacks write permission on the file or the `/var/log/app` directory.\n\nFix:\n1. Run `ls -ld /var/log/app /var/log/app/app.log*` to check the current owner.\n2. Identify the user that runs the rotation process.\n3. Run `chown -R user:group /var/log/app` to assign ownership to that user.\n4. Run `chmod 755 /var/log/app` to grant write access to the directory.", "usage": {"input": 75054, "output": 1223, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 76277, "reasoningTokens": 1067, "cost": {"input": 0.150108, "output": 0.014676, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.16478399999999999}}, "cost_usd": 0.164784}
